request.description:
Stream ball events in real-time for a specific match using Server-Sent Events (SSE). This endpoint streams ball additions as they happen via Redis Streams. Connect using EventSource in JavaScript:

```javascript
const eventSource = new EventSource('http://localhost:8080/api/v1/sse/matches/{match_id}/balls');

eventSource.addEventListener('connected', (e) => {
  console.log('Connected:', JSON.parse(e.data));
});

eventSource.addEventListener('ball_added', (e) => {
  const ballEvent = JSON.parse(e.data);
  console.log('Ball added:', ballEvent);
  // Update your UI with the ball event data
});

eventSource.onerror = (err) => {
  console.error('SSE Error:', err);
};
```

Event types:
- `connected`: Initial connection confirmation
- `ball_added`: Ball event with all ball details
- `: heartbeat`: Keep-alive message (every 30 seconds)

Note: This is a streaming endpoint that keeps the connection open. In Postman, you'll see the connection remain active until you cancel it.

Stream all match events in real-time for a specific match using Server-Sent Events (SSE). This endpoint streams all types of match events via Redis Streams. Connect using EventSource in JavaScript:

```javascript
const eventSource = new EventSource('http://localhost:8080/api/v1/sse/matches/{match_id}/events');

eventSource.addEventListener('connected', (e) => {
  console.log('Connected:', JSON.parse(e.data));
});

eventSource.addEventListener('ball_added', (e) => {
  const ballEvent = JSON.parse(e.data);
  console.log('Ball added:', ballEvent);
});

eventSource.addEventListener('match_event', (e) => {
  const matchEvent = JSON.parse(e.data);
  console.log('Match event:', matchEvent);
});

eventSource.onerror = (err) => {
  console.error('SSE Error:', err);
};
```

Event types:
- `connected`: Initial connection confirmation
- `ball_added`: Ball event with all ball details
- `match_event`: Generic match events
- `: heartbeat`: Keep-alive message (every 30 seconds)

Note: This is a streaming endpoint that keeps the connection open. In Postman, you'll see the connection remain active until you cancel it.

